CAT = "oacpReport"; SEG = "RPT"
Q = [
("Occurrence report: At 14:20 on May 3, Constable Ruth Okafor responded to a shoplifting call at Northgate Hardware, 88 Lakeshore Road, Barrie. The manager, Dev Singh, said a man in a grey hoodie took two cordless drills and left on foot heading east. Singh valued the drills at $340. No one was hurt. Okafor viewed store video showing the man leaving at 14:05. Who valued the stolen drills?", "Dev Singh, the manager", ["Constable Ruth Okafor", "The man in the grey hoodie", "Northgate's head office"], "The report says Singh valued the drills at $340. Okafor took the report and viewed the video but gave no value."),
("Dispatch note: At 22:40 a caller reported a car in a ditch on Concession 6 near Orillia. Unit 12 was sent at 22:43 and arrived at 22:58. The driver, Lena Fischer, was not hurt. A tow truck was called at 23:05 and arrived at 23:40. Unit 12 cleared the scene at 23:52. How long after the call did Unit 12 arrive?", "18 minutes", ["15 minutes", "58 minutes", "25 minutes"], "The call came at 22:40 and the unit arrived at 22:58, which is 18 minutes. Fifteen minutes counts from when the unit was sent, not from the call."),
("Witness Marco Lima: \"The van was white and drove off north on Elm Street. The driver had a thick beard.\" Witness Joy Park: \"A white van drove off north on Elm. The driver was clean-shaven and wore a red cap.\" Both were standing outside the Sudbury post office. On which detail do the two witnesses disagree?", "The driver's facial hair", ["The colour of the van", "The direction the van went", "The street the van used"], "Lima says the driver had a beard and Park says clean-shaven. Both agree the van was white and went north on Elm."),
("Report: On June 9 at 08:15, Constable Amir Haddad stopped a blue pickup on Highway 7 in Peterborough for having no rear licence plate. The driver, Carla Ruiz, said the plate had fallen off that morning. Haddad found the plate on the truck's back seat and gave Ruiz a warning. Which summary sentence is most accurate?", "Stopped for no rear plate; driver was warned", ["Stopped for speeding; driver was charged", "Stopped for speeding; truck was towed", "Stopped for no rear plate; truck was towed"], "The stop was for the missing plate and the outcome was a warning. No charge was laid, and Haddad found the plate on the back seat; nothing says the truck was towed."),
("Statement of Paul Dorsey, 61: \"I locked my garage on Hillcrest Avenue at 9 p.m. When I woke at 6 a.m., the side window was broken and my snowblower was gone. My neighbour's dog barks at strangers, but I heard nothing all night. I sleep with earplugs.\" Based only on this statement, what can be concluded?", "The theft happened overnight", ["The neighbour's dog was quiet", "The thief knew the dog well", "The garage door was forced open"], "The garage was secure at 9 p.m. and the snowblower was gone by 6 a.m. Dorsey hearing nothing proves little about the dog, since he wore earplugs."),
("Service policy says every found property report must list the owner's name, a description of the item, its estimated value and where it was found. Report: \"A black leather wallet was found by a cyclist on the trail behind Riverside Arena, Guelph. It was handed in at 16:10. The owner is Tom Beaudry.\" Which required item is missing?", "The estimated value", ["The owner's name", "Where it was found", "A description of the item"], "The report names the owner, describes a black leather wallet and says it was on the trail. It never gives a value."),
("Notes from Constable Sara Kim at 12 Pine Crescent, Belleville, written out of order: (1) Called an ambulance after checking his breathing. (2) Arrived at the house at 03:10. (3) Found Ed Marsh on the kitchen floor. (4) Paramedics took Marsh to hospital at 03:32. Which order is correct?", "2, 3, 1, 4", ["3, 2, 1, 4", "2, 1, 3, 4", "1, 2, 3, 4"], "She arrived, found Marsh, checked him and called the ambulance, and then paramedics took him. The call could not come before finding him, since it followed checking his breathing."),
("Report: At 19:30 on October 2, a resident of 41 Maple Drive, Kingston, called to say her parked car had been keyed. Constable Neil Brandt arrived at 19:52 and saw a long scratch along the driver's door. The owner, Rita Cohen, said she parked on the street at 17:00 and noticed the damage at 19:15. Based on Cohen's account, when was the car damaged?", "Between 17:00 and 19:15", ["Between 19:15 and 19:30", "Between 19:30 and 19:52", "Between 15:00 and 17:00"], "The car was undamaged when parked at 17:00 and damaged when she noticed at 19:15. The times after 19:15 are when she called and when police came."),
("Report by Constable Leah Brooks: \"At 11:05 I saw a green sedan run the red light at Main and Queen in North Bay. I followed it east on Queen and stopped it at 11:09. The driver, Owen Pratt, gave me his licence. After issuing a warning to the driver of the red sedan, I returned to the station at 11:40.\" Which detail in the report does not match?", "The colour of the car", ["The time of the stop", "The direction it went", "The name of the driver"], "The car is called green at the start and red at the end. The time, direction and driver are each given only once, so they cannot conflict."),
("Witness Hana Ito: \"Two men ran out of the bank on Front Street at about 10:15. The taller one carried a black bag.\" Witness Raj Patel: \"At about 10:20, two men came out of the bank running. One had a black backpack, and they got into a silver car.\" On which point do both witnesses agree?", "The number of men", ["The time they fled", "Who carried the bag", "The colour of the car"], "Both say two men. Ito says 10:15 and Patel 10:20, and only Patel mentions a car."),
("Dispatch note: Caller Mia Rossi, 22 Birch Lane, Sault Ste. Marie, reports loud music from the house next door since 23:00. She says about 30 cars are parked on the street and one is blocking her driveway. She does not want the neighbours to know she called. Unit 7 assigned at 00:15. Which of these does the note state?", "A car is blocking her driveway", ["The music started at midnight", "Unit 7 arrived at 00:15", "The caller gave a false name"], "Rossi says one car is blocking her driveway. Unit 7 was assigned at 00:15; the note does not say when it arrived."),
("Report: Store clerk Ben Adeyemi says the cash drawer at a Cornwall bakery was $200 short at closing on Friday. Only he and the owner, Grace Lin, opened the drawer that day. Lin counted the drawer at noon and it balanced. She was away from the store from noon until closing. If these facts are true, who was the only person able to open the drawer after it last balanced?", "Ben Adeyemi, the clerk", ["Grace Lin, the owner", "Both Lin and Adeyemi", "A customer at the till"], "Only the two of them opened the drawer, and Lin was away from noon on. That leaves Adeyemi as the only one who could open it after the noon count."),
("Report: Constable Dana Wells was sent to a collision on Highway 11 near Huntsville at 16:02. She arrived at 16:11 and closed one lane. The fire service arrived at 16:15 and freed a trapped passenger at 16:40. The road reopened at 17:25. How long was the passenger trapped after the fire service arrived?", "25 minutes", ["29 minutes", "38 minutes", "45 minutes"], "From 16:15 to 16:40 is 25 minutes. Twenty-nine minutes counts from Wells's arrival at 16:11 instead."),
("Witness statement of Ivan Petrov: \"I was walking my dog on Ridge Road at about 7 a.m. A red hatchback came round the bend too fast, hit the curb and knocked over a mailbox. The driver got out, looked at it, then drove off toward Highway 400. I did not see the plate.\" Which summary is most accurate?", "A hatchback hit a mailbox and left", ["A van hit a mailbox and stayed", "A hatchback hit a fence and stayed", "A van hit a fence and left"], "Petrov says a hatchback knocked over a mailbox and drove off. The driver got out only briefly before leaving, and nothing was said about a fence."),
("Report: Constable Theo Grant took a theft report from Lisa Moreau at 13:00 on Tuesday. Moreau said her bicycle was locked outside the Kitchener library from 09:00. She came out at 12:30 and found the lock cut and the bike gone. A library worker, Sam Liu, said he saw the bike there at 11:45. Based on these accounts, when was the bicycle taken?", "Between 11:45 and 12:30", ["Between 09:00 and 11:45", "Between 12:30 and 13:00", "Between 11:00 and 11:45"], "Liu saw the bike at 11:45 and it was gone by 12:30. Before 11:45 is ruled out by Liu's sighting."),
("Dispatch note: \"Unit 3 sent to 140 Oak Street, Thunder Bay, for a fall, 09:12.\" Officer's report: \"At 09:20 I arrived at 140 Oak Avenue. I found Mrs. June Hall, 82, on the floor of her porch. Paramedics arrived at 09:27 and took her to hospital.\" Which detail differs between the note and the report?", "The address of the call", ["The reason for the call", "The time the unit was sent", "The age of the woman"], "The note says Oak Street and the report says Oak Avenue. The time sent and the age each appear in only one of them, so they cannot differ."),
("Statement of Nadia Farah: \"I parked my car at the Ajax GO station lot at 7:10 a.m. and took the train. When I got back at 6:20 p.m., my rear window was smashed and my laptop bag was gone. I had left the bag on the back seat where anyone could see it.\" What does Farah's statement show?", "The bag was in plain view", ["She locked all the doors", "The car was hit in the morning", "Other cars were damaged too"], "She says the bag was on the back seat where anyone could see it. She gives no time of the theft beyond the day she was away."),
("Constable Ali Shah's notes from Dundas Street, London, written out of order: (1) She called for a tow truck. (2) The tow truck left with the car. (3) She saw a car stalled across two lanes. (4) The tow truck arrived. Which order is correct?", "3, 1, 4, 2", ["3, 4, 1, 2", "1, 3, 4, 2", "3, 1, 2, 4"], "She saw the car, called for a tow, the truck arrived and then it left with the car. The truck cannot arrive before it was called."),
("Report: On March 14, Constable Marie Tremblay received a fraud complaint from Gordon Elliott, 74, of Belleville. Elliott said a caller claiming to be his grandson asked for $2,000 for bail. Elliott's daughter, Kim, stopped him before he went to the bank. No money was lost. Who stopped the payment?", "Elliott's daughter, Kim", ["Constable Marie Tremblay", "A teller at the bank", "Elliott's real grandson"], "The report says Kim stopped her father before he reached the bank. Tremblay only took the complaint afterwards."),
("Witness Omar Said: \"The fight started outside the bar on King Street at 1:30 a.m. The man in the blue jacket threw the first punch.\" Witness Beth Carey: \"I saw it begin at 1:30. The man in the black jacket swung first, then the man in blue hit back.\" What do the witnesses disagree about?", "Who threw the first punch", ["When the fight started", "How many men fought", "What the men were wearing"], "Said blames the man in blue and Carey the man in black. Both put the start at 1:30."),
("Service policy says a tow report must list the plate number, the reason for the tow, the tow company and the time towed. Report: \"Plate CBRX 412. Towed for blocking a fire route at Parkway Mall, Hamilton. Officer: Constable Jean Roy. Time towed: 15:40.\" Which required item is missing?", "The tow company", ["The plate number", "The reason for the tow", "The time towed"], "The plate, reason and time are all listed. No tow company is named."),
("Report: At 20:10, Constable Kofi Mensah checked on a man asleep in a parked car at a Windsor gas station. The man, Glen Hart, said he was resting before a long drive. Mensah saw no sign of alcohol, the engine was off, and a records check showed Hart was not wanted. Mensah left at 20:25. Which is the most accurate summary?", "A resting driver checked; no issue found", ["A sleeping driver was arrested at 20:25", "A driver slept in a running car, impaired", "A wanted man was found asleep in a car"], "Mensah found nothing wrong and left. The engine was off, there was no sign of alcohol and Hart was not wanted."),
("Dispatch log, Cobourg: 02:14 alarm at Harbour Pharmacy. 02:16 Unit 5 sent. 02:24 Unit 5 on scene, rear door found open. 02:31 Unit 5 asks for a K9 unit. 02:52 K9 unit on scene. 03:20 owner arrives to secure the door. How long did Unit 5 wait for the K9 unit after asking for it?", "21 minutes", ["28 minutes", "36 minutes", "38 minutes"], "The request was at 02:31 and the K9 unit arrived at 02:52, which is 21 minutes. Twenty-eight minutes counts from 02:24, before the request."),
("Statement of Wendy Clarke: \"I came home to my apartment in Mississauga at 5:45 p.m. The door was unlocked, though I am sure I locked it at 8 a.m. My jewellery box was open and empty. My roommate, Ana, has a key but was at work all day.\" Which statement is supported by Clarke's account?", "The jewellery box was empty", ["Ana took the jewellery", "The door lock was broken", "The break-in was in the morning"], "Clarke says the box was open and empty. She does not say the lock was broken, and she gives no time for the break-in."),
("Report: Constable Iris Novak attended a house party complaint at 1 Cedar Court, Waterloo, at 23:30. She counted about 60 guests. The host, Liam Byrne, 23, agreed to turn the music down. Novak returned at 00:45 after a second call and found the music loud again. She gave Byrne a noise warning. Why did Novak return to the house?", "A second complaint came in", ["To count the guests again", "Byrne asked her to come back", "To check on Byrne's age"], "She returned at 00:45 after a second call. Nothing says Byrne asked her back."),
("Statement of Carl Mott: \"I left the Sarnia arena at 9:30 p.m. and stopped for a coffee on the way. I got home at 10:30 and found my front window smashed. I called police right away, at about 9:45.\" Which part of Mott's statement does not fit the rest?", "The time he called police", ["The time he left the arena", "The coffee stop on the way", "The smashed front window"], "He says he called right after getting home at 10:30, yet gives 9:45, before he was home. The coffee stop fits the hour between leaving and arriving."),
("Statement of Pia Lund: \"At noon I was waiting for a bus on Market Street in Brantford. A tall man in a green coat walked along the parked cars and tried three door handles. He seemed nervous. He then walked into the bus terminal and I lost sight of him.\" Which part of the statement is an opinion rather than an observation?", "That he seemed nervous", ["That he wore a green coat", "That he tried door handles", "That he entered the terminal"], "Seeming nervous is Lund's judgment of his mood. The coat, the door handles and entering the terminal are things she saw."),
("Report: At 10:40 on August 21, Constable Yusuf Abdi took a complaint from Helen Grieve at her farm stand on County Road 2 near Brockville. Grieve said a man paid for a basket of corn with a $50 bill that a counterfeit detection pen later marked as fake. She described him as about 40, wearing a straw hat, and driving a brown pickup with a ladder rack. What did the man buy?", "A basket of corn", ["A ladder rack", "A straw hat", "A counterfeit pen"], "Grieve says he paid for a basket of corn. The ladder rack was on his truck and the hat was what he wore."),
]
